            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Buckwheat Queen"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I liked this tea even though I'm not big on the liquorice taste of fennel. I used some tea from tea bags I got in a hotel room, I figured you can't get cheaper than that. I've never been on an Indian train, but something tells me there should be some ginger in this. It is nice and re-heats well. Thank you KitchenBarbarian for this recipe."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "mysterioso"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I put whole ingredients in a mortar and crushed them a little to get more of the flavor in the tea. Used almond milk and Splenda for sweetness.",
            "datePublished": "2026-07-12T15:32:31.208Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Audrey Noyb"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was good, though I did sub in almond coconut blend for dairy and tweaked the spices. Used ground cardamom because it’s what I had inn the house, and increased the proportion ( love that cardamom flavor!). Added a sliver of fresh ginger and a piece of cinnamon stick. Boiled the spices a few minutes longer before adding the “milk”. Sweetened with Swerve. Smells and tastes lovely And is keto/diabetes friendly😀",
            "datePublished": "2022-12-07T00:50:51.677Z"
          }
